    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 2.0,
      "end": 8.0,
      "text": "In the night sky, the moon seems rather small, but in reality, it really isn't.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.14076,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.021896
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 8.0,
      "end": 10.0,
      "text": "Central Europe would easily fit under it.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.14076,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.021896
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 10.0,
      "end": 13.0,
      "text": "The surface area of the moon is huge.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.14076,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.021896
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 13.0,
      "end": 17.0,
      "text": "To give you some perspective, it's as big as the whole European continent,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.14076,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.021896
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 17.0,
      "end": 21.0,
      "text": "China, the USA, Brazil and South Africa together.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.14076,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.021896
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 21.0,
      "end": 26.0,
      "text": "Weight-wise, the moon is only about 181th of the mass of Earth.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.14076,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.021896
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 26.0,
      "end": 28.0,
      "text": "But how big is it in relation to Earth?",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.14076,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.021896
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 28.0,
      "end": 30.0,
      "text": "Quite big, actually.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.082579,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.001115
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 30.0,
      "end": 34.0,
      "text": "Our moon is the biggest in the solar system in relation to its planet.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.082579,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.001115
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 34.0,
      "end": 40.0,
      "text": "And it's the fifth largest moon in the solar system, quite a bit bigger than the dwarf planet Pluto.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.082579,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.001115
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 40.0,
      "end": 47.0,
      "text": "Now, if the moon is really that huge, how far away is it from us to seem this small in the night sky?",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.082579,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.001115
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 47.0,
      "end": 51.0,
      "text": "370 kilometers, as far as the ISS maybe?",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.082579,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.001115
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 51.0,
      "end": 56.0,
      "text": "No, at that distance, gravitational forces would rip the moon apart.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.082579,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.001115
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 56.0,
      "end": 61.0,
      "text": "At 36,000 kilometers, it would be as far away as our most distant satellites.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.065275,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.000404
    }
  ],
